{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/603299-fluctuations-of-the-gauntlet-rating","id":603299,"title":"Fluctuations of the Gauntlet Rating","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-25T17:12:04-07:00","id":603299,"title":"Fluctuations of the Gauntlet Rating","content":"The rules as written seem to imply the Gauntlet is mostly &quot;fixed&quot;. Of course, changes in the environment eventually are reflected in the Gauntlet, but this usually slow and long term. However, the Gauntler for any said area is usually the same. In Wraith, the Shroud operates similarly in mechanics, but the books of that line talk about various times when the rating of the Shroud lowers or increases (like on Halloween). I think Werewolf should be similar.<br /> <br /> Foklore and magic often mention appropriate times or places when magic is performed, or when beings from the Other Realms cross over. These are liminal times and places - not one thing or the other, but a mix, and this breakdown in order allows... things to happen. I think this would be a good time for the Gauntlet to decrease, and to compensate other times that are much &quot;stronger&quot; in one way, the Gauntlet might even rise.<br /> <br /> For example, the changes in the seasons are good time for when the Gauntlet could be lowered.<ul><li>The solstices and equinoxes and their relevant seasonal celebrations (Imbolc/Candlemas, Walpurgis Night/Beltane, Lammas/Lugnasa, and Samhain/All Soul's Day) could have a Gauntlet rating of minus one than normal.</li> <li>Certains hours of the day would also be good. Twilight and dawn are appropriate. We also have times like Midnight, &quot;the witching hour&quot;, or &quot;hour of the wolf&quot; when the Gauntlet might be lowered - but only for Wyrm creatures.</li> <li>There are also liminal places like crossroads, caverns, bridges, springs, and coastlines. All could lower the Gauntlet by one.</li> </ul><br /> I like this because it would drive behavior. Garou and other beings of magic would want to hold important rituals and such that work better with a lowered gauntlet at these special times and places. This is what happens in folklore and stories. This isn't what I usually see at the gaming table though. I think it would improve the game, but making it seem more like how people believe the occult to be in the real world. It doesn't penalize anyone in their normal roleplay, but gives them options if they want the benefit. It also is a way to increase tension when fighting the bad guys as the ST could use the date of the next seasonal equinox or whatever as the obvious time for the bad guys to perform their plot device ritual, and the PCs know they are under the gun to find and stop them before that.<br /> <br /> Has anyone does this in their own games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T17:34:38-07:00","id":603325,"title":"","content":"Location-based Gauntlet changes aren't really fluctuations. They're just reflecting a different place with a lower Gauntlet than another location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T18:01:47-07:00","id":603337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/603299-fluctuations-of-the-gauntlet-rating?p=603325#post603325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Location-based Gauntlet changes aren't really fluctuations. They're just reflecting a different place with a lower Gauntlet than another location.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood, however, the rules as is really don't make a distinction between the variety within one location. So I think your comment - while true - misses the point. &quot;Rural countryside&quot; is Gauntlet difficulty rating 6. If you want lower, the obvious thing is to go into Deep Wilderness or to a caern. This is how most people think with the rules as written. <br /> <br /> However, if one believes that certain locations by their nature has the advantageous of certain geographic features, the world opens up. You can have an advantage if you find that cave or lakeshore in the rural countryside which further reduces difficulty by 1. You don't need to go outside the area to a &quot;deep wilderness&quot; or a &quot;caern&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you want to technically call it &quot;fluctuations within a Gauntlet Chart Area&quot; instead of the Gauntlet, go ahead.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T18:58:56-07:00","id":603362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/603299-fluctuations-of-the-gauntlet-rating?p=603337#post603337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Understood, however, the rules as is really don't make a distinction between the variety within one location. So I think your comment - while true - misses the point. &quot;Rural countryside&quot; is Gauntlet difficulty rating 6. If you want lower, the obvious thing is to go into Deep Wilderness or to a caern. This is how most people think with the rules as written.<br /> <br /> However, if one believes that certain locations by their nature has the advantageous of certain geographic features, the world opens up. You can have an advantage if you find that cave or lakeshore in the rural countryside which further reduces difficulty by 1. You don't need to go outside the area to a &quot;deep wilderness&quot; or a &quot;caern&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you want to technically call it &quot;fluctuations within a Gauntlet Chart Area&quot; instead of the Gauntlet, go ahead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't. That's the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T23:21:30-07:00","id":603539,"title":"","content":"A real world example of how I think the rule works:<br /> I live in a city my neighborhood is a mix of residential and industrial. The chart would indicate a 8. I work in an artificial Industrial park nice green very suburban feel with the ducks, rabbits, fox, and even the red tailed hawks a 7. If I run over the field behind work and through the corn field while feeling rural it isn't if however I continue in the same direction about 15 miles I hit a stretch that has so far avoided development and is all farms and fields or rural enough to be a 6. <br /> The gauntlet in the game is a mystic barrier that reflects the Triats influence and Gaia's on the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T18:28:03-07:00","id":605164,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that the Shroud and various magical effects are somewhat tied to human perception, and sure, the Umbra itself reflects emotions in some cases, but the Gauntlet is much more mechanical than that. Is there a reason that pattern spiders stay away from this particular cave or lake? They're not superstitious. Is there some powerful spiritual effect that's fighting them off (maybe counterproductive), or fooling them, or actively working its own chaos? Then sure, maybe. Otherwise no.<br /> <br /> I think of the Gauntlet as expanding like sand...if you have some very high gauntlet area like a research lab in a city, you're pouring a lot of sand on that spot, and it's spreading out around it. If you try to make a low gauntlet area, you're digging out sand, and more keeps pouring in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T20:07:23-07:00","id":605250,"title":"","content":"One concept -- and a very critical one, in my opinion -- from early on (up to 1994/5) that got lost pretty quickly is that the barriers of the Gauntlet (Middle-Penumbral), the Shroud (Low Umbral) and the Astral Gauntlet (to the High Umbra) were similar-but-separate things, metaphysically. That is, for example, the Gauntlet to the Middle Umbra in the city may be an 8 or 9, depending on location; however, the Shroud rating at the city cemetery might be a 6, even though it's located in the same geographical area. On the flip, the Gauntlet might be a 5 to enter the MU along a bright, secluded island cove that is largely untouched by civilization (a few huts, simple boats, but not luxury hotel, etc.) -- especially if the character attempts to enter the MU by crossing into the cove or sailing out towards the horizon of the sea; the Shroud there, though, might be an 8 or even 9 due to the ambient forces of life and light that the place happens to embody. That city example might include a very high rating to enter the High Umbra as with the other layers of the Umbrae... save that, in the old college building -- and particularly the centuries-old, intact library that has stood for centuries -- the Gauntlet to the High Umbra might only be a 6 vs. the 9 one might expect for the MU or LU in possibly the same area. <br /> <br /> This idea, which is metaphysically much more sound than a more &quot;streamlined&quot; Gauntlet/Shroud, reflects the differences between the various Umbrae, as well as takes into account *concept* as well as locality when it comes to metaphysical influences. It's a shame it got mostly simplified. My friends and I have stuck with the original alluded idea, and it really has given things a more &quot;legit&quot; feeling over the years by allowing the individual aspects of the various &quot;penumbral connections&quot; to make more sense relative to their expressed concepts.<br /> <br /> Food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T20:15:24-07:00","id":605254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/603299-fluctuations-of-the-gauntlet-rating#post603299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Foklore and magic often mention appropriate times or places when magic is performed, or when beings from the Other Realms cross over. These are liminal times and places - not one thing or the other, but a mix, and this breakdown in order allows... things to happen. I think this would be a good time for the Gauntlet to decrease, and to compensate other times that are much &quot;stronger&quot; in one way, the Gauntlet might even rise.<br /> <br /> For example, the changes in the seasons are good time for when the Gauntlet could be lowered.<ul><li>The solstices and equinoxes and their relevant seasonal celebrations (Imbolc/Candlemas, Walpurgis Night/Beltane, Lammas/Lugnasa, and Samhain/All Soul's Day) could have a Gauntlet rating of minus one than normal.</li> <li>Certains hours of the day would also be good. Twilight and dawn are appropriate. We also have times like Midnight, &quot;the witching hour&quot;, or &quot;hour of the wolf&quot; when the Gauntlet might be lowered - but only for Wyrm creatures.</li> <li>There are also liminal places like crossroads, caverns, bridges, springs, and coastlines. All could lower the Gauntlet by one.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>That's more or less how it works in the Dark Ages setting, particularly for DA:Mage, wherein time of day (twilight/dawn, night vs. day, etc.) can influence when the Gauntlet/Shroud is a little stronger or a little weaker (stronger during the day, weaker at night, crossroads and &quot;inbetween places/times&quot; being a little more flexible than at other times/places, et al.). In the Modern Era(s), though, it does make more sense that the general ratings of the Gauntlet/Shroud (relative to themselves) should remain pretty consistent in terms of geography: the world has become much more static and removed from what it was before, and mystical &quot;by-ways&quot; aren't nearly as influential as they used to be. Of course, in *your* game, they may still be, and that's as legitimate as anyone else's setting. (However, keep in mind that certain metaphysical side-effects come hand-in-hand with that as a matter of intuitive sense -- there'd be a few more &quot;legit&quot; hauntings/manifestations than occur &quot;normally&quot; in the WoD, as presented, and similar such. Just something to keep in mind...)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T21:23:04-07:00","id":605270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/603299-fluctuations-of-the-gauntlet-rating?p=605254#post605254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's more or less how it works in the Dark Ages setting, particularly for DA:Mage, wherein time of day (twilight/dawn, night vs. day, etc.) can influence when the Gauntlet/Shroud is a little stronger or a little weaker (stronger during the day, weaker at night, crossroads and &quot;inbetween places/times&quot; being a little more flexible than at other times/places, et al.). In the Modern Era(s), though, it does make more sense that the general ratings of the Gauntlet/Shroud (relative to themselves) should remain pretty consistent in terms of geography: the world has become much more static and removed from what it was before, and mystical &quot;by-ways&quot; aren't nearly as influential as they used to be. Of course, in *your* game, they may still be, and that's as legitimate as anyone else's setting. (However, keep in mind that certain metaphysical side-effects come hand-in-hand with that as a matter of intuitive sense -- there'd be a few more &quot;legit&quot; hauntings/manifestations than occur &quot;normally&quot; in the WoD, as presented, and similar such. Just something to keep in mind...)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-HUwLA57paU\" target=\"_blank\">WHAT A WONDERFUL<br /> NIGHT TO STEP<br /> SIDEWAYS</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T03:40:15-07:00","id":605438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/603299-fluctuations-of-the-gauntlet-rating?p=605270#post605270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-HUwLA57paU\" target=\"_blank\">WHAT A WONDERFUL<br /> NIGHT TO STEP<br /> SIDEWAYS</a></div> </div> </div> </div>... Wait, Konami ripped off the cover for Castle Ravenloft for that? :P<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.giantbomb.com/uploads/original/3/31838/2178861-cv2_offart8.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://db4sgowjqfwig.cloudfront.net/assets/287480/strahd__1_.jpg?1390516143\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T08:19:04-07:00","id":605615,"title":"","content":"lol<br /> <br /> *So* funny! (Sidenote: I happen to being running a very loosely intermingled DA meets Ravenloft game for a couple of friends; it's a variation of what I've been doing since WoD came out 25 years ago. I'd been running variations of Ravenloft since the original module game out back in '83, when I first started gaming... &gt;stops to reflect on that statement for a moment&lt; #TheOldness )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T09:57:52-07:00","id":605669,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go sit in my rocking chair now since I'm feeling #TheOldness as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:39:11-07:00","id":610269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/603299-fluctuations-of-the-gauntlet-rating?p=605164#post605164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason that pattern spiders stay away from this particular cave or lake? They're not superstitious. Is there some powerful spiritual effect that's fighting them off (maybe counterproductive), or fooling them, or actively working its own chaos? Then sure, maybe. Otherwise no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the powerful spiritual effect is that they are naturally liminal, and thus the Gauntlet right there will always be weaker than the surrounding area. Think of it like a natural sinkhole. No matter how much sand or concrete is poured, this area is going cause some of it to sink. To continue the metaphor, if the Pattern Spider is pouring a concrete foundation over that area, then this one spot is going to be deformed or defective compared to the rest.<br /> <br /> Maybe not all such areas are sufficient to reduce area's Gauntlet by an entire one point; it can be something the ST can use to distinguish certain areas where the liminality is more apparent - this stretch of the shoreline as opposed to just any shoreline. But I still like it as another tool to give to the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  Corrected some grammar 08-03-2015, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:41:25-07:00","id":610271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/603299-fluctuations-of-the-gauntlet-rating?p=605250#post605250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One concept -- and a very critical one, in my opinion -- from early on (up to 1994/5) that got lost pretty quickly is that the barriers of the Gauntlet (Middle-Penumbral), the Shroud (Low Umbral) and the Astral Gauntlet (to the High Umbra) were similar-but-separate things, metaphysically.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I run it. The things that define the level of the Gauntlet, Shroud, or whatever are different. So it is possible for a Hospital to be haunted (low Shroud rating), even if the hospital is in an urban area that would have a high Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T19:33:36-07:00","id":612905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/603299-fluctuations-of-the-gauntlet-rating?p=610271#post610271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how I run it. The things that define the level of the Gauntlet, Shroud, or whatever are different. So it is possible for a Hospital to be haunted (low Shroud rating), even if the hospital is in an urban area that would have a high Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Plenty of earlier citations (various rules-mechanics indicators) as well as fluff went in that direction; it wasn't until in later parts of the 2nd Ed. era -- and solidly in the Revised/3rd Ed. era -- that they streamlined things for ease of interaction. While I understand that on a conceptual rules level, the error in metaphysical thought/perspective is annoying... especially for a game setting that stays pretty &quot;deep&quot; compared to most other RPGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T19:56:41-07:00","id":612926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/603299-fluctuations-of-the-gauntlet-rating?p=612905#post612905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Plenty of earlier citations (various rules-mechanics indicators) as well as fluff went in that direction; it wasn't until in later parts of the 2nd Ed. era -- and solidly in the Revised/3rd Ed. era -- that they streamlined things for ease of interaction. While I understand that on a conceptual rules level, the error in metaphysical thought/perspective is annoying... especially for a game setting that stays pretty &quot;deep&quot; compared to most other RPGs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting off by saying that I'm not trying to be argumentative, just asking for clarification <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You start off by saying &quot;Exactly.&quot; in response to Black Fox saying that the rules that govern each spiritual barrier are different. And then you seem to go on to say that having the rules be different is an error (&quot;the error in metaphysical thought/perspective is annoying&quot;).<br /> <br /> So do you agree that the rules are/should be different for different barriers (in this case, mostly talking about the Shroud and the Gauntlet)? Like....since time of day/year affect the Shroud, do you think there should be the possibility timing doing something to the Gauntlet rating?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T07:01:30-07:00","id":615006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/603299-fluctuations-of-the-gauntlet-rating?p=612926#post612926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Starting off by saying that I'm not trying to be argumentative, just asking for clarification <img src=\"https://foru