ey <b>streamlined things for ease of interaction</b></i>. While I understand <b><i>that </i></b>on a conceptual rules level, the error in metaphysical thought/perspective is annoying... especially for a game setting that stays pretty &quot;deep&quot; compared to most other RPGs.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Do you see where you were misreading? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}